{"t": "ention", "lp": -0.00038452388253062963, "top": [["ention", -0.00038452388253062963], ["ENTION", -8.618775367736816]]}, {"t": "ally", "lp": -0.527804970741272, "top": [["ally", -0.527804970741272], ["al", -0.8931652307510376]]}, {"t": ",", "lp": -0.5136732459068298, "top": [[",", -0.5136732459068298], [")", -1.1750426292419434]]}, {"t": " per", "lp": -0.5473597645759583, "top": [[" per", -0.5473597645759583], [" see", -1.1353609561920166]]}, {"t": " `", "lp": -0.01874762959778309, "top": [[" `", -0.01874762959778309], [" options", -4.3635735511779785]]}, {"t": "!", "lp": -0.0130601292476058, "top": [["!", -0.0130601292476058], ["options", -4.462830066680908]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). This is standard practice in build functions.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n| Flag | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **Source directory** \u2014 where the source code lives |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **Build directory** \u2014 where build artifacts go |\n| `-G Ninja` | Use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, efficient) |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Optimize build with `-O3`-style flags, no debug symbols |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Install location root |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Put libraries in `/usr/lib` (not `/usr/lib64`) |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel's **C** compiler |\n| `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx` | Use Intel's **C++** compiler |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=` | Empty \u2192 **disable** ccache/compilad (intentionally, per `!"}